/* Baustein ar: Articles and quantifiers. Automatisch erzeugt, nicht von Hand ändern. */
GT_UNIT({"id":"ar","title":"Articles and quantifiers","ruleTitle":"Articles and quantifiers","date":"2026-10-06","sets":{"b":[{"n":"a, an or the?","p":["b1"]},{"n":"the or no article?","p":["b2"]}],"k":[{"n":"Countable or uncountable?","p":["k1"]},{"n":"some or any?","p":["k2"]}],"p":[{"n":"few or little?","p":["p1"]},{"n":"Fixed phrases and names","p":["p2"]}]},"tags":{"AN":"a oder an (nach dem Laut), a / an bei Berufen","TH":"a / an oder the (neu oder schon bekannt, einmalig)","ZA":"Kein Artikel bei Allgemeinem (life, music, people)","UN":"Unzählbare Nomen (advice, information, homework)","MM":"much oder many","SA":"some oder any","FL":"(a) few oder (a) little","FP":"Feste Wendungen ohne Artikel (go to bed, by bus)","GN":"Artikel bei geografischen Namen"},"coach":"Before you choose, ask yourself whether the listener knows which one you mean. If not, you need a or an. If so, you need the. And if you mean things in general, you need no article at all.","quips":{"AN":["It is the sound that decides, not the letter. An hour, but a uniform.","In English a job needs a or an. She is a pilot, and he is an actor."],"TH":["The first time it is a, and after that it is the, because now we both know which one."],"ZA":["Things in general take no article. Life, love and music manage very well without the.","I used to live in a garden, so trust me on this one: nature takes no article, and it has a lot of snails."],"UN":["Advice, information and homework never take -s, however much of them you get."],"MM":["Can you count it? Then it is many. If you can't, it is much."],"SA":["Some is for positive sentences, and any is for negatives and questions.","When you ask for something or offer something, you say some."],"FL":["The small word a changes everything. A few means some, and few means almost none.","Few goes with things you can count, and little goes with things you can't."],"FP":["Go to bed, by bus, have lunch: these phrases travel without an article."],"GN":["Rivers, seas and mountain ranges take the. Most countries, cities and lakes don't."]},"tasks":{"b1":"Add a, an or the.","b2":"With the or without?","bc":"a, an, the or no article?","k2":"some or any?","p1":"a few, few, a little or little?","p2":"With the or without?","pc":"With the or without?"},"card":{"top":["Does the listener know which one you mean?","No → a / an. Yes → the. Things in general → no article."],"lines":[{"s":"b1","r":"an + vowel sound, otherwise a","e":"{an} <<apple>> · {an} <<hour>> ^silent h^ // {a} <<dog>> · {a} <<uniform>> ^like \"you\"^","n":"Jobs take a / an: She is {a} <<teacher>>."},{"s":"b1","r":"New → a / an. Already known → the.","e":"I saw {a} <<fox>> last night. {The} <<fox>> was eating pizza.","n":"There is only one: {the} <<sun>> · {the} <<internet>>"},{"s":"b2","r":"Things in general → no article","e":"I love <<music>>. ^music in general^ // {The} <<music>> at the party was terrible. ^this music^","n":"German trap „Das Leben ist hart.“ → <<Life>> is hard. // Also: most <<people>> ~the most people~"},{"s":"k1","r":"Uncountable: no a / an, no plural -s","e":"Can I give you some <<advice>>? // I need more <<information>>.","n":"Not: ~an advice~ · ~informations~ // Also: homework, news, furniture, luggage, luck, fun"},{"s":"k1","r":"much + uncountable · many + plural","e":"How {much} <<time>> do we have? // How {many} <<people>> are coming?"},{"s":"k2","r":"some → positive sentences · any → negatives and questions","e":"I have {some} <<snacks>>. // I do not have {any} <<money>>. · Do you have {any} <<ideas>>?","n":"Offers and requests take some: Would you like {some} <<tea>>? // Same for something / anything and someone / anyone"},{"s":"p1","r":"a few / a little = some · few / little = almost none","e":"I have {a few} <<ideas>>. ^some^ · I have {few} <<ideas>>. ^almost none^ // We have {a little} <<time>>. ^some^ · We have {little} <<time>>. ^almost none^","n":"few + plural · little + uncountable"},{"s":"p2","r":"No article: go to bed, go home","e":"I go to <<school>> by <<bus>>. // We had <<breakfast>> at <<home>>.","n":"Also: go to work, at night, next week // play football · but: play {the} <<guitar>>"},{"s":"p2","r":"Rivers, seas, mountain ranges → the","e":"{the} <<Rhine>>, {the} <<Atlantic>>, {the} <<Alps>>","n":"Also: {the} <<USA>>, {the} <<UK>>, {the} <<Netherlands>> // No article: Germany, Berlin, Lake Garda"}],"key":"<<blue>> noun · {red} article or quantity word · [yellow] signal word"},"lessons":{"b1":{"t":"a, an or the?","s":[{"b":"{an} <<apple>> · {a} <<dog>>","t":"English has two words for \"ein\" and \"eine\": a and an. An comes before a vowel sound, because the two words are easier to say together that way."},{"b":"{an} <<apple>> · {an} <<hour>> ^silent h^ // {a} <<dog>> · {a} <<uniform>> ^like \"you\"^","t":"It is the sound that counts, not the letter. Hour starts with a silent h, so it is an hour. Uniform starts with a sound like \"you\", so it is a uniform."},{"b":"Sie ist Lehrerin. // She is {a} <<teacher>>. ~She is teacher.~","t":"Here is a German trap. In English a job always takes a or an: She is a teacher. He is an engineer.","m":"dry"},{"b":"I saw {a} <<fox>> last night.","t":"Now the difference between a and the. The first time you mention something, it is new for the listener. That takes a or an."},{"b":"I saw {a} <<fox>> last night. {The} <<fox>> was eating pizza.","t":"After that, the listener knows which fox you mean. Now it is the fox."},{"b":"{the} <<sun>> · {the} <<internet>> · {the} best <<player>>","t":"Some things are known from the start, because there is only one of them: the sun, the internet, the best player in the team."}],"k":[[{"b":"He works as ___ electrician.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["a","an","the"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. Electrician starts with a vowel sound.","w":"No. Electrician starts with a vowel sound, and jobs take a or an: He works as an electrician."},{"b":"She goes to ___ European school.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["a","an"],"c":0,"r":"Right. European sounds like \"you\" at the start.","w":"No. European starts with a sound like \"you\", so it takes a: a European school."}],[{"b":"I bought {a} <<game>> yesterday. {The} <<game>> is brilliant.","t":"Why \"The game\" in the second sentence?","o":["Because the listener now knows which game.","Because games are expensive.","Because the sentence is short."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Once it has been mentioned, it takes the.","w":"No. The game was mentioned before, so the listener knows which one you mean. That takes the."},{"b":"We met {a} <<girl>> from Spain. {The} <<girl>> spoke perfect German.","t":"Why \"a girl\" in the first sentence?","o":["Because she is from Spain.","Because she is new for the listener.","Because girl is a short word."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. The first time you mention somebody, you use a or an.","w":"No. The listener has not heard of her before. Something new takes a or an."}]]},"b2":{"t":"the or no article?","s":[{"b":"I love <<music>>. ^music in general^","t":"When you talk about things in general, English uses no article at all. Music here means all music, everywhere."},{"b":"I love <<music>>. ^music in general^ // {The} <<music>> at the party was terrible. ^this music^","t":"The comes back as soon as you mean one special thing. The music at the party is not all music. It is this music."},{"b":"<<Dogs>> are loyal. ^all dogs^ // {The} <<dogs>> next door bark all night. ^these dogs^","t":"It works the same with plural nouns. Dogs are all dogs. The dogs next door are two very special dogs."},{"b":"Das Leben ist hart. // <<Life>> is hard. ~The life is hard.~","t":"German loves the article here: das Leben, die Liebe, die Natur, die Zeit. English leaves it out.","m":"dry"},{"b":"most <<people>> ~the most people~","t":"One more for the list: \"die meisten Leute\" is most people, without the."}],"k":[[{"b":"___ is more important than money.","t":"Which fits?","o":["Health","The health","A health"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. Health in general takes no article.","w":"No. This is about health in general, and that takes no article: Health is more important than money."},{"b":"___ you cooked yesterday were delicious.","t":"Which fits?","o":["Vegetables","The vegetables","A vegetables"],"c":1,"r":"Right. These are special vegetables, the ones from yesterday.","w":"No. You mean the vegetables from yesterday, not vegetables in general. That takes the."}],[{"b":"<<Children>> ask a lot of questions.","t":"Why is there no \"the\" before \"children\"?","o":["Because it is about children in general.","Because children is an irregular plural.","Because the sentence is positive."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Things and people in general take no article.","w":"No. The sentence is about all children in general, and that takes no article."},{"b":"{The} <<children>> in my street are very loud.","t":"Why \"The children\" here?","o":["Because children are always loud.","Because it is about one special group of children.","Because the sentence starts with it."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. One special group takes the.","w":"No. These are not children in general. They are the children in one street, and one special group takes the."}]]},"k1":{"t":"Countable or uncountable?","s":[{"b":"one <<idea>> · two <<ideas>> · three <<ideas>>","t":"Most nouns can be counted: one idea, two ideas. They have a plural, and they can take a or an."},{"b":"<<water>> · <<money>> · <<music>> · <<time>>","t":"Some nouns cannot be counted. You do not say two waters or three moneys. These nouns have no plural, and they never take a or an."},{"b":"Can I give you some <<advice>>? ~an advice~ ~advices~ // I need more <<information>>. ~informations~","t":"The dangerous ones are the nouns that German can count: ein Rat, eine Information, eine Hausaufgabe. In English advice, information and homework are uncountable.","m":"dry"},{"b":"<<homework>> · <<news>> · <<furniture>> · <<luggage>> · <<weather>> · <<luck>> · <<fun>>","t":"These belong to the same group. If you want to count one of them, you need a helper: a piece of advice, a piece of information."},{"b":"How {much} <<time>> do we have? // How {many} <<people>> are coming?","t":"The same difference decides between much and many. Much goes with uncountable nouns, and many goes with plural nouns."},{"b":"{a lot of} <<time>> · {a lot of} <<people>>","t":"A lot of fits both, and in a positive sentence it is what people usually say: I have a lot of time."}],"k":[[{"b":"How ___ sleep did you get?","t":"Which word fits?","o":["much","many"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. Sleep is uncountable.","w":"No. You cannot count sleep, so it takes much: How much sleep did you get?"},{"b":"How ___ songs do you know by heart?","t":"Which word fits?","o":["much","many"],"c":1,"r":"Right. Songs is a plural noun.","w":"No. Songs is a plural noun, so it takes many: How many songs do you know by heart?"}],[{"b":"She gave me some <<advice>>.","t":"Why \"some advice\" and not \"an advice\"?","o":["Because advice is uncountable.","Because she is older.","Because some sounds more polite."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. An uncountable noun never takes a or an.","w":"No. Advice is uncountable in English, so it cannot take a or an."},{"b":"We have too {much} <<homework>>.","t":"Why \"much\" and not \"many\"?","o":["Because it is a negative sentence.","Because homework is uncountable.","Because too comes before it."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Much goes with uncountable nouns.","w":"No. Homework is uncountable, and uncountable nouns take much."}]]},"k2":{"t":"some or any?","s":[{"b":"I have {some} <<snacks>>.","t":"Some and any both stand for an amount that is not exact. Which one you need depends on the kind of sentence. A positive sentence takes some."},{"b":"I have {some} <<snacks>>. // I do not have {any} <<money>>. · Do you have {any} <<ideas>>?","t":"Negative sentences and questions take any."},{"b":"Would you like {some} <<tea>>? · Can I have {some} <<chips>>?","t":"There is one exception. When you offer something or ask for something, you say some, even though it is a question. You expect the answer yes."},{"b":"{something} · {someone} // {anything} · {anyone}","t":"The longer words follow the same rule. There is something in my shoe. There isn’t anything in the fridge."}],"k":[[{"b":"There aren't ___ buses after midnight.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["some","any"],"c":1,"r":"Yes. A negative sentence takes any.","w":"No. This is a negative sentence, and negatives take any: There aren’t any buses after midnight."},{"b":"I found ___ old photos in the attic.","t":"Which word fits?","o":["some","any"],"c":0,"r":"Right. A positive sentence takes some.","w":"No. This is a positive sentence, and that takes some: I found some old photos in the attic."}],[{"b":"Could I have {some} <<bread>>, please?","t":"Why \"some\" in a question?","o":["Because it is a request.","Because bread is uncountable.","Because please comes at the end."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Requests and offers take some.","w":"No. This is a request. When you ask for something or offer something, you say some."},{"b":"We do not have {any} <<milk>>.","t":"Why \"any\" and not \"some\"?","o":["Because milk is uncountable.","Because the sentence is negative.","Because we comes first."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. A negative sentence takes any.","w":"No. The sentence is negative, and negatives take any."}]]},"p1":{"t":"few or little?","s":[{"b":"{many} <<ideas>> · {much} <<time>>","t":"You know many for plural nouns and much for uncountable nouns. The words for small amounts come in the same two kinds."},{"b":"{few} <<ideas>> · {little} <<time>>","t":"Few goes with plural nouns, and little goes with uncountable nouns."},{"b":"I have {a few} <<ideas>>. ^some^ · I have {few} <<ideas>>. ^almost none^","t":"Now look at the small word a. A few ideas means some ideas, and that is good news. Few ideas means almost none, and that is a problem."},{"b":"We have {a little} <<time>>. ^some^ · We have {little} <<time>>. ^almost none^","t":"Little works in the same way. A little time is enough for a coffee. Little time means you have to run."},{"b":"can you count it? → {few} · can't you? → {little} // some → with {a} · almost none → without {a}","t":"So you ask two questions. Can you count it? And is it some, or almost none?"}],"k":[[{"b":"I have ___ friends in Berlin, so I am never bored there.","t":"Which fits?","o":["a few","few","a little"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. Friends is a plural noun, and the speaker has some.","w":"No. The speaker is never bored, so there are some friends. Friends is a plural noun: a few friends."},{"b":"There is ___ water in the bottle. Take a sip.","t":"Which fits?","o":["a few","little","a little"],"c":2,"r":"Right. Water is uncountable, and there is some.","w":"No. There is enough for a sip, so there is some. Water is uncountable: a little water."}],[{"b":"He has {little} <<money>>.","t":"What does this sentence tell you?","o":["He is almost broke.","He has some money, and that is enough.","He has a lot of coins."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Little means almost none.","w":"No. Without a, little means almost none. He is almost broke."},{"b":"She has {a few} <<questions>>.","t":"What does this sentence tell you?","o":["She has almost no questions.","She has some questions.","She has too many questions."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. A few means some.","w":"No. A few means some. Without a, it would mean almost none."}]]},"p2":{"t":"Fixed phrases and names","s":[{"b":"I go to <<school>> by <<bus>>.","t":"Some everyday phrases have no article at all, and they are fixed. You go to school, to work and to bed, and you travel by bus, by car or by train."},{"b":"I go to <<school>> by <<bus>>. // We had <<breakfast>> at <<home>>.","t":"Meals take no article either: breakfast, lunch, dinner. You are at home, at school and at work, you go home, and you sleep at night."},{"b":"mit dem Bus → by <<bus>> ~with the bus~ // nächste Woche → next <<week>> ~the next week~","t":"German puts an article into most of these, so translating word by word goes wrong. The same is true for last week and next year.","m":"dry"},{"b":"play <<football>> · watch <<TV>> // but: play {the} <<guitar>>","t":"Sports take no article, and neither does TV. Musical instruments are the exception: you play the guitar, the piano, the drums."},{"b":"<<Germany>> · <<Berlin>> · <<Lake Garda>>","t":"Now names. Most countries, cities and lakes take no article."},{"b":"{the} <<Rhine>>, {the} <<Atlantic>>, {the} <<Alps>>","t":"Rivers, seas and mountain ranges are different. They always take the."},{"b":"{the} <<USA>>, {the} <<UK>>, {the} <<Netherlands>>","t":"A few countries take the as well: the ones with a plural name, or with a word like States or Kingdom in the name."}],"k":[[{"b":"We went to Paris by ___.","t":"Which fits?","o":["train","the train","a train"],"c":0,"r":"Yes. By train has no article.","w":"No. For transport you say by train, without an article: We went to Paris by train."},{"b":"My sister plays ___ in the school band.","t":"Which fits?","o":["trumpet","the trumpet","a trumpet"],"c":1,"r":"Right. Instruments take the.","w":"No. Musical instruments take the: My sister plays the trumpet in the school band."}],[{"b":"{The} <<Danube>> flows through <<Vienna>>.","t":"Why \"The Danube\", but only \"Vienna\"?","o":["Because rivers take the, and cities take no article.","Because the Danube is very long.","Because the sentence starts with it."],"c":0,"r":"Exactly. Rivers take the, and cities don’t.","w":"No. Rivers always take the, and cities take no article."},{"b":"She lives in {the} <<USA>>, and her brother lives in <<Canada>>.","t":"Why \"the USA\", but only \"Canada\"?","o":["Because the USA is further away.","Because USA has the word States in it.","Because Canada is colder."],"c":1,"r":"Exactly. Names with States or Kingdom take the.","w":"No. Most countries take no article, like Canada. The USA has the word States in its name, and that takes the."}]]}},"items":[{"i":"e-01","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"It took us ___ (a / an) hour to find the right platform.","f":"","g":"","a":[["an"]],"h":["an"]},{"i":"e-02","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"My mum is ___ (nurse / a nurse), so we have breakfast at very strange times.","f":"","g":"","a":[["a nurse"]],"h":["a nurse"]},{"i":"e-03","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I love ___ (nature / the nature), but I hate insects. It is complicated.","f":"","g":"","a":[["nature"]],"h":["nature"]},{"i":"e-04","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"We watched a film last night. ___ (A / The) film was so bad that we started laughing.","f":"","g":"","a":[["The"]],"h":["The"]},{"i":"e-05","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"How ___ (much / many) homework did we get? I stopped listening after the word \"essay\".","f":"","g":"","a":[["much"]],"h":["much"]},{"i":"e-06","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"Can you give me ___ (an advice / some advice)? I have never been to a job interview.","f":"","g":"","a":[["some advice"]],"h":["some advice"]},{"i":"e-07","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I don't have ___ (some / any) money on me. Can you pay?","f":"","g":"","a":[["any"]],"h":["any"]},{"i":"e-08","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"There are too ___ (much / many) people in this lift. I can hear it thinking.","f":"","g":"","a":[["many"]],"h":["many"]},{"i":"e-09","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I have ___ (few / a few) questions. Do you have a minute?","f":"","g":"","a":[["a few"]],"h":["a few"]},{"i":"e-10","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"There is ___ (little / a little) hope left. We are losing 0–5, and there are two minutes to go.","f":"","g":"","a":[["little"]],"h":["little"]},{"i":"e-11","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"I usually go to school ___ (with the bus / by bus), but today my dad drove me.","f":"","g":"","a":[["by bus"]],"h":["by bus"]},{"i":"e-12","s":"e","t":"gap","x":"My cousin has lived in ___ (Netherlands / the Netherlands) for three years.","f":"","g":"","a":[["the Netherlands"]],"h":["the Netherlands"]},{"i":"b1-01","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"My cousin wants to be ___ engineer, but she can't even fix her own bike.","f":"\"Engineer\" starts with a vowel sound, so it is \"an\". Jobs always take a or an.","g":"AN","c":"an","w":["a","the"]},{"i":"b1-02","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"We waited for ___ hour, and then the concert was cancelled.","f":"The h in \"hour\" is silent, so the word starts with a vowel sound: an hour.","g":"AN","c":"an","w":["a","the"]},{"i":"b1-03","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"She studies at ___ university in Scotland.","f":"\"University\" sounds like \"you\" at the start, so it is \"a\".","g":"AN","c":"a","w":["an"]},{"i":"b1-04","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"I found ___ wallet on the bus. ___ wallet had no money in it, only a photo of a dog.","f":"The first time you mention it, it is new: a wallet. After that the listener knows which one: the wallet.","g":"TH","c":"a … The","w":["the … A","a … A"]},{"i":"b1-05","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Don't look directly at ___ sun. Even my little brother knows that.","f":"There is only one sun, so everybody knows which one you mean: the sun.","g":"TH","c":"the","w":["a","an"]},{"i":"b1-06","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Somebody asks about your dad's job. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Jobs take a or an in English: a bus driver.","g":"AN","c":"My dad is a bus driver.","w":["My dad is bus driver.","My dad is an bus driver."]},{"i":"b1-07","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"Can I ask you ___ honest question? Do you actually like my haircut?","f":"The h in \"honest\" is silent, so it is \"an honest question\".","g":"AN","c":"an","w":["a","the"]},{"i":"b1-08","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"There is ___ strange man outside our house. I think ___ man is looking for his cat.","f":"New for the listener: a strange man. Then you both know which one: the man.","g":"TH","c":"a … the","w":["the … a","a … a"]},{"i":"b1-09","s":"b1","t":"mc","x":"I looked it up on ___ internet, so it must be true.","f":"There is only one internet, so it is \"the internet\".","g":"TH","c":"the","w":["an","a"]},{"i":"b1-10","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"My sister is ___ (actor). So far she has played a tree and a dead body.","f":"Jobs take a or an, and \"actor\" starts with a vowel sound: an actor.","g":"AN","a":[["an actor"]],"h":["an actor"]},{"i":"b1-11","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"I need ___ (new phone). Mine switches itself off when it sees 20 per cent.","f":"It is new for the listener, and \"new\" starts with a consonant sound: a new phone.","g":"TH","a":[["a new phone"]],"h":["a new phone"]},{"i":"b1-12","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"We have ___ (MP3 player) from 2009 at home. My dad calls it vintage.","f":"You say \"em-pee-three\", so the word starts with a vowel sound: an MP3 player.","g":"AN","a":[["an MP3 player"]],"h":["an MP3 player"]},{"i":"b1-13","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"Can you close ___ (door)? Everybody can hear us.","f":"You both know which door you mean, so it is \"the door\".","g":"TH","a":[["the door"]],"h":["the door"]},{"i":"b1-14","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"I saw a cat and a dog in the park. ___ (dog) was afraid of ___ (cat).","f":"You have already mentioned them, so the listener knows which ones: the dog, the cat.","g":"TH","a":[["The dog"],["the cat"]],"h":["The dog","the cat"]},{"i":"b1-15","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"He wears ___ (uniform) at work, and he loves it a bit too much.","f":"\"Uniform\" sounds like \"you\" at the start, so it is \"a uniform\".","g":"AN","a":[["a uniform"]],"h":["a uniform"]},{"i":"b1-16","s":"b1","t":"gap","x":"___ (moon) looks huge tonight. Come outside!","f":"There is only one moon, so it is \"the moon\".","g":"TH","a":[["The moon"]],"h":["The moon"]},{"i":"b1-17","s":"b1","t":"fix","x":"My mum is *teacher*, so she knows every excuse.","f":"Jobs take a or an in English: a teacher.","g":"AN","a":[["a teacher"]],"h":["a teacher"]},{"i":"b1-18","s":"b1","t":"fix","x":"It was *an* expensive mistake, but at least nobody filmed it.","f":"\"Expensive\" starts with a vowel sound, so \"an\" is correct.","g":"AN","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"b2-01","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"You are complaining about the wifi. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Life in general takes no article.","g":"ZA","c":"Life is too short for bad wifi.","w":["The life is too short for bad wifi.","A life is too short for bad wifi."]},{"i":"b2-02","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Somebody asks why you have no pet. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Dogs in general take no article.","g":"ZA","c":"I love dogs, but my flat is too small.","w":["I love the dogs, but my flat is too small.","I love a dogs, but my flat is too small."]},{"i":"b2-03","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"I like the film, but ___ is awful. Who chose these songs?","f":"You mean the music in this one film, so it is \"the music\".","g":"ZA","c":"the music","w":["music","a music"]},{"i":"b2-04","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence is about all teenagers in general?","f":"Without an article you mean teenagers in general. \"The teenagers\" would be one special group.","g":"ZA","c":"Teenagers hate getting up early.","w":["The teenagers hate getting up early."]},{"i":"b2-05","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"You are talking about the start of the week. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"Most people\" takes no article.","g":"ZA","c":"Most people hate Mondays.","w":["The most people hate Mondays.","Most of people hate Mondays."]},{"i":"b2-06","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Can you pass me ___, please? It is right next to your elbow.","f":"You can both see which salt you mean, so it is \"the salt\".","g":"ZA","c":"the salt","w":["salt","a salt"]},{"i":"b2-07","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Somebody asks about your favourite subject. Which sentence is correct?","f":"School subjects are things in general, so they take no article: history.","g":"ZA","c":"History is my favourite subject.","w":["The history is my favourite subject.","A history is my favourite subject."]},{"i":"b2-08","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"Thank you for ___ you lent me last week. I will pay you back soon. Probably.","f":"You mean one special amount, the money from last week, so it is \"the money\".","g":"ZA","c":"the money","w":["money","a money"]},{"i":"b2-09","s":"b2","t":"mc","x":"You have a theory about money. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Money, happiness and pizza in general take no article.","g":"ZA","c":"Money can't buy happiness, but it can buy pizza.","w":["The money can't buy the happiness, but it can buy the pizza.","Money can't buy the happiness, but it can buy pizza."]},{"i":"b2-10","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"___ (love) is blind, and in my sister's case it is also deaf.","f":"Love in general takes no article.","g":"ZA","a":[["Love"]],"h":["Love"]},{"i":"b2-11","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"I can't hear the film. Can you tell ___ (children) to be quiet?","f":"You both know which children you mean, so it needs \"the\".","g":"ZA","a":[["the children"]],"h":["the children"]},{"i":"b2-12","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"My brother is afraid of ___ (spiders). He once slept in the car because of one.","f":"Spiders in general take no article.","g":"ZA","a":[["spiders"]],"h":["spiders"]},{"i":"b2-13","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"___ (weather) in this city has a personal problem with me.","f":"You mean the weather in one place, so it needs \"the\".","g":"ZA","a":[["The weather"]],"h":["The weather"]},{"i":"b2-14","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"Many people say that ___ (time) is money. My little brother has plenty of both, apparently.","f":"Time in general takes no article.","g":"ZA","a":[["time"]],"h":["time"]},{"i":"b2-15","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"___ (films) are my hobby, but ___ (film) we saw last night was two hours of nothing.","f":"Films in general take no article. \"The film we saw last night\" is one special film.","g":"ZA","a":[["Films"],["the film"]],"h":["Films","the film"]},{"i":"b2-16","s":"b2","t":"gap","x":"\"I am not interested in ___ (politics),\" says my cousin, and then he complains about bus prices for an hour.","f":"Politics in general takes no article.","g":"ZA","a":[["politics"]],"h":["politics"]},{"i":"b2-17","s":"b2","t":"fix","x":"*The nature* is beautiful, but it has too many mosquitoes.","f":"Nature in general takes no article.","g":"ZA","a":[["Nature"]],"h":["Nature"]},{"i":"b2-18","s":"b2","t":"fix","x":"Could you turn off *the light*? I am trying to sleep.","f":"You both know which light you mean, so \"the light\" is correct.","g":"ZA","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"bc-01","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"My brother wants to be ___ astronaut or ___ YouTuber. He is keeping his options open.","f":"\"Astronaut\" starts with a vowel sound: an. \"YouTuber\" sounds like \"you\" at the start: a.","g":"AN","c":"an … a","w":["a … a","an … an"]},{"i":"bc-02","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence is about school in general?","f":"Without an article you mean school in general. \"The school\" would be one special building.","g":"ZA","c":"School starts far too early.","w":["The school starts far too early."]},{"i":"bc-03","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"I bought ___ jacket yesterday, but ___ jacket has a hole in it. I am taking it back.","f":"First it is new for the listener: a jacket. Then you both know which one: the jacket.","g":"TH","c":"a … the","w":["the … a","a … a"]},{"i":"bc-04","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"She is ___ best drummer in our school, and she knows it.","f":"There is only one best drummer, so it is \"the\".","g":"TH","c":"the","w":["a","an"]},{"i":"bc-05","s":"bc","t":"mc","x":"We live in ___ old house with ___ huge garden.","f":"\"Old\" starts with a vowel sound: an old house. \"Huge\" starts with a consonant sound: a huge garden.","g":"AN","c":"an … a","w":["a … a","an … an"]},{"i":"bc-06","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"My aunt is ___ (pilot), and she still gets lost in car parks.","f":"Jobs take a or an in English: a pilot.","g":"AN","a":[["a pilot"]],"h":["a pilot"]},{"i":"bc-07","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"___ (sleep) is important. That is my excuse, and I am keeping it.","f":"Sleep in general takes no article.","g":"ZA","a":[["Sleep"]],"h":["Sleep"]},{"i":"bc-08","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"Have you seen ___ (remote control)? It was on the sofa a minute ago.","f":"You both know which remote control you mean, so it is \"the\".","g":"TH","a":[["the remote control"]],"h":["the remote control"]},{"i":"bc-09","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"I waited for half ___ (hour), and then I ate your chips. Sorry.","f":"The h in \"hour\" is silent, so it is \"an hour\".","g":"AN","a":[["an hour"]],"h":["an hour"]},{"i":"bc-10","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"I really like ___ (chocolate), but ___ (chocolate) in this cake tastes like soap.","f":"Chocolate in general takes no article. The chocolate in this one cake needs \"the\".","g":"ZA","a":[["chocolate"],["the chocolate"]],"h":["chocolate","the chocolate"]},{"i":"bc-11","s":"bc","t":"fix","x":"My uncle is *an* electrician, so our lights never work. He has no time.","f":"\"Electrician\" starts with a vowel sound, and jobs take a or an.","g":"AN","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"bc-12","s":"bc","t":"gap","x":"I read ___ (interesting article) about sharks last night. ___ (article) said that they are older than trees.","f":"New for the listener: an interesting article. Then you both know which one: the article.","g":"TH","a":[["an interesting article"],["The article"]],"h":["an interesting article","The article"]},{"i":"k1-01","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"How ___ water do you drink a day? Coffee does not count.","f":"\"Water\" is uncountable, so it is \"how much\".","g":"MM","c":"much","w":["many","a lot"]},{"i":"k1-02","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"How ___ followers does your dog have? More than me, I guess.","f":"\"Followers\" is a plural noun, so it is \"how many\".","g":"MM","c":"many","w":["much","a lot"]},{"i":"k1-03","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"You are planning a class trip. Which sentence is correct?","f":"\"Information\" is uncountable: no \"an\" and no plural -s.","g":"UN","c":"I need some information about the hostel.","w":["I need an information about the hostel.","I need some informations about the hostel."]},{"i":"k1-04","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"My grandma gave me ___ before my first date.","f":"\"Advice\" is uncountable: no \"a\" and no plural -s.","g":"UN","c":"some good advice","w":["a good advice","some good advices"]},{"i":"k1-05","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"We had ___ at the party. Nobody wanted to go home.","f":"\"Fun\" is uncountable, so it cannot take \"many\" or \"a\". \"A lot of\" fits every noun.","g":"UN","c":"a lot of fun","w":["many fun","a fun"]},{"i":"k1-06","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"There are too ___ adverts in this video. I have forgotten what I wanted to watch.","f":"\"Adverts\" is a plural noun, so it is \"too many\".","g":"MM","c":"many","w":["much","a lot"]},{"i":"k1-07","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"We bought ___ for my room at the weekend. Now I can't find the floor.","f":"\"Furniture\" is uncountable: no \"a\" and no plural -s.","g":"UN","c":"some new furniture","w":["a new furniture","some new furnitures"]},{"i":"k1-08","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"I don't have ___ homework today, so I can finally do nothing.","f":"\"Homework\" is uncountable, so it is \"much\".","g":"MM","c":"much","w":["many","a lot"]},{"i":"k1-09","s":"k1","t":"mc","x":"She travels with so ___ luggage that she needs her own bus.","f":"\"Luggage\" is uncountable, so it is \"so much\".","g":"MM","c":"much","w":["many","a lot"]},{"i":"k1-10","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"How ___ (much / many) sugar do you want in your tea? Say when.","f":"\"Sugar\" is uncountable, so it is \"how much\".","g":"MM","a":[["much"]],"h":["much"]},{"i":"k1-11","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"How ___ (much / many) times have I told you not to touch my charger?","f":"\"Times\" is a plural noun here, so it is \"how many\".","g":"MM","a":[["many"]],"h":["many"]},{"i":"k1-12","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"Do you have ___ (an information / any information) about the new teacher?","f":"\"Information\" is uncountable, so it cannot take \"an\".","g":"UN","a":[["any information"]],"h":["any information"]},{"i":"k1-13","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"We did not have ___ (much / many) luck with the weather. It rained on all six days.","f":"\"Luck\" is uncountable, so it is \"much\".","g":"MM","a":[["much"]],"h":["much"]},{"i":"k1-14","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"Let me give you ___ (an advice / a piece of advice): never read the comments.","f":"\"Advice\" is uncountable. For one, you say \"a piece of advice\".","g":"UN","a":[["a piece of advice"]],"h":["a piece of advice"]},{"i":"k1-15","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"There is not ___ (much / many) furniture in my room: a bed, a desk and a chair that I use as a wardrobe.","f":"\"Furniture\" is uncountable, so it is \"much\".","g":"MM","a":[["much"]],"h":["much"]},{"i":"k1-16","s":"k1","t":"gap","x":"I got so ___ (much / many) messages last night that my phone gave up.","f":"\"Messages\" is a plural noun, so it is \"so many\".","g":"MM","a":[["many"]],"h":["many"]},{"i":"k1-17","s":"k1","t":"fix","x":"I have to do a lot of *homeworks* tonight, so I can't come.","f":"\"Homework\" is uncountable, so it has no plural -s.","g":"UN","a":[["homework"]],"h":["homework"]},{"i":"k1-18","s":"k1","t":"fix","x":"How *much* money do you need for the trip?","f":"\"Money\" is uncountable, so \"how much\" is correct.","g":"MM","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"k2-01","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"I have ___ good news and ___ bad news. Which do you want first?","f":"A positive sentence takes \"some\".","g":"SA","c":"some … some","w":["any … any","some … any"]},{"i":"k2-02","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Sorry, there isn't ___ milk left. Somebody put the empty carton back in the fridge.","f":"A negative sentence takes \"any\".","g":"SA","c":"any","w":["some","a"]},{"i":"k2-03","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Do you have ___ brothers or sisters, or are you the lucky one?","f":"A normal question takes \"any\".","g":"SA","c":"any","w":["some","a"]},{"i":"k2-04","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Would you like ___ grapes? They are a bit soft, but they are free.","f":"An offer takes \"some\", even though it is a question.","g":"SA","c":"some","w":["a","much"]},{"i":"k2-05","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Can I have ___ water, please? That chilli was a mistake.","f":"A request takes \"some\", even though it is a question.","g":"SA","c":"some","w":["any","a"]},{"i":"k2-06","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"There is ___ strange in the fridge. It is green, and I think it moved.","f":"A positive sentence takes \"something\".","g":"SA","c":"something","w":["anything","some"]},{"i":"k2-07","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"I didn't know ___ at the party, so I talked to the dog all evening.","f":"A negative sentence takes \"anyone\".","g":"SA","c":"anyone","w":["someone","any"]},{"i":"k2-08","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"The kitchen is empty again. Which sentence is correct?","f":"A negative sentence takes \"any\".","g":"SA","c":"We don't have any bread.","w":["We don't have some bread.","We have not some bread."]},{"i":"k2-09","s":"k2","t":"mc","x":"Are there ___ questions? No? Good, because I don't know the answers.","f":"A normal question takes \"any\".","g":"SA","c":"any","w":["some","a"]},{"i":"k2-10","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"I need ___ new headphones. My brother sat on the old ones.","f":"A positive sentence takes \"some\".","g":"SA","a":[["some"]],"h":["some"]},{"i":"k2-11","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"We can't make pancakes. We don't have ___ eggs.","f":"A negative sentence takes \"any\".","g":"SA","a":[["any"]],"h":["any"]},{"i":"k2-12","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"Have you got ___ idea how late it is? The neighbours are standing at the door.","f":"A normal question takes \"any\".","g":"SA","a":[["any"]],"h":["any"]},{"i":"k2-13","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"Can I borrow ___ paper? I left my whole bag on the bus.","f":"A request takes \"some\", even though it is a question.","g":"SA","a":[["some"]],"h":["some"]},{"i":"k2-14","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"There are ___ biscuits in the cupboard, but there isn't ___ chocolate. I checked twice.","f":"The first part is positive: some. The second part is negative: any.","g":"SA","a":[["some"],["any"]],"h":["some","any"]},{"i":"k2-15","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"I haven't seen ___ good films this year. Maybe I am getting old.","f":"A negative sentence takes \"any\".","g":"SA","a":[["any"]],"h":["any"]},{"i":"k2-16","s":"k2","t":"gap","x":"Mum, can we have ___ pizza tonight? I will even lay the table.","f":"A request takes \"some\", even though it is a question.","g":"SA","a":[["some"]],"h":["some"]},{"i":"k2-17","s":"k2","t":"fix","x":"I don't have *some* time today, but tomorrow is fine.","f":"A negative sentence takes \"any\".","g":"SA","a":[["any"]],"h":["any"]},{"i":"k2-18","s":"k2","t":"fix","x":"Would you like *some* soup? You look frozen.","f":"An offer takes \"some\", so it is correct here.","g":"SA","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"kc-01","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"How ___ money is left on your card? We still need tickets for the way back.","f":"\"Money\" is uncountable, so it is \"how much\".","g":"MM","c":"much","w":["many","a lot"]},{"i":"kc-02","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"I asked for ___ about the course, and they sent me forty pages.","f":"\"Information\" is uncountable: no \"an\" and no plural -s.","g":"UN","c":"some information","w":["an information","some informations"]},{"i":"kc-03","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"There aren't ___ seats left, so we will have to stand.","f":"A negative sentence takes \"any\".","g":"SA","c":"any","w":["some","much"]},{"i":"kc-04","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"You are eating chips. Which sentence is correct?","f":"A request takes \"some\", even though it is a question.","g":"SA","c":"Could I have some ketchup, please?","w":["Could I have any ketchup, please?","Could I have a ketchup, please?"]},{"i":"kc-05","s":"kc","t":"mc","x":"We don't have ___ time, and there are far too ___ things on this list.","f":"\"Time\" is uncountable: much. \"Things\" is a plural noun: many.","g":"MM","c":"much … many","w":["many … much","much … much"]},{"i":"kc-06","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"How ___ (much / many) hours did you sleep? You look like a ghost.","f":"\"Hours\" is a plural noun, so it is \"how many\".","g":"MM","a":[["many"]],"h":["many"]},{"i":"kc-07","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"I don't want ___ (some / any) trouble. I only want my ball back.","f":"A negative sentence takes \"any\".","g":"SA","a":[["any"]],"h":["any"]},{"i":"kc-08","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"That is ___ (a good news / good news)! When do you start?","f":"\"News\" is uncountable, so it cannot take \"a\".","g":"UN","a":[["good news"]],"h":["good news"]},{"i":"kc-09","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"There is ___ (some / any) juice in the fridge, but don't drink it from the bottle.","f":"A positive sentence takes \"some\".","g":"SA","a":[["some"]],"h":["some"]},{"i":"kc-10","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"She did not give me ___ (much / many) advice. She just said \"good luck\" and left.","f":"\"Advice\" is uncountable, so it is \"much\".","g":"MM","a":[["much"]],"h":["much"]},{"i":"kc-11","s":"kc","t":"fix","x":"Our new flat is nice, but we need more *furnitures*.","f":"\"Furniture\" is uncountable, so it has no plural -s.","g":"UN","a":[["furniture"]],"h":["furniture"]},{"i":"kc-12","s":"kc","t":"gap","x":"Do you have ___ (some / any) pets? I have ___ (some / any) fish, but they are not very talkative.","f":"A normal question takes \"any\". A positive sentence takes \"some\".","g":"SA","a":[["any"],["some"]],"h":["any","some"]},{"i":"p1-01","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"I have ___ suggestions for your profile picture. First of all, delete it.","f":"\"Suggestions\" is a plural noun, and the speaker has some: a few.","g":"FL","c":"a few","w":["few","a little"]},{"i":"p1-02","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"There is ___ milk left, enough for your coffee.","f":"\"Milk\" is uncountable, and there is some: a little.","g":"FL","c":"a little","w":["little","a few"]},{"i":"p1-03","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"He has ___ friends in his new town, so he spends most evenings alone.","f":"\"Friends\" is a plural noun, and he has almost none: few.","g":"FL","c":"few","w":["a few","little"]},{"i":"p1-04","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"My grandad has ___ patience with slow internet. He shouts at the router.","f":"\"Patience\" is uncountable, and he has almost none: little.","g":"FL","c":"little","w":["a little","few"]},{"i":"p1-05","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence means that the speaker has some money?","f":"\"A little\" means \"some\". \"Little\" means \"almost none\".","g":"FL","c":"I have a little money.","w":["I have little money."]},{"i":"p1-06","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"Can you wait ___ minutes? I am nearly ready.","f":"\"Minutes\" is a plural noun, and you mean some: a few minutes.","g":"FL","c":"a few","w":["few","a little"]},{"i":"p1-07","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence means that almost nobody came?","f":"\"Few\" means \"almost none\". \"A few\" means \"some\".","g":"FL","c":"Few people came to the meeting.","w":["A few people came to the meeting."]},{"i":"p1-08","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"I speak ___ Spanish, enough to order food and say sorry.","f":"\"Spanish\" is uncountable, and the speaker knows some: a little.","g":"FL","c":"a little","w":["little","a few"]},{"i":"p1-09","s":"p1","t":"mc","x":"Very ___ people in my class have ever written a letter. I am one of them, and it was to Santa.","f":"\"People\" is a plural noun, and there are almost none: very few.","g":"FL","c":"few","w":["a few","little"]},{"i":"p1-10","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I only have ___ euros left, but that is enough for chips.","f":"\"Euros\" is a plural noun, and there are some: a few.","g":"FL","a":[["a few"]],"h":["a few"]},{"i":"p1-11","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"Add ___ salt. Not too much, last time it tasted like the sea.","f":"\"Salt\" is uncountable, and you mean some: a little.","g":"FL","a":[["a little"]],"h":["a little"]},{"i":"p1-12","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"There are ___ shops in our village, so we drive to town for almost everything.","f":"\"Shops\" is a plural noun, and there are almost none: few.","g":"FL","a":[["few"]],"h":["few"]},{"i":"p1-13","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"She had ___ interest in football, so she read a book during the final.","f":"\"Interest\" is uncountable, and she had almost none: little.","g":"FL","a":[["little"]],"h":["little"]},{"i":"p1-14","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"I have seen ___ episodes, and I already love it. Don't tell me who dies.","f":"\"Episodes\" is a plural noun, and the speaker has seen some: a few.","g":"FL","a":[["a few"]],"h":["a few"]},{"i":"p1-15","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"There is very ___ space in my room. I have to move the chair to open the door.","f":"\"Space\" is uncountable, and there is almost none: very little.","g":"FL","a":[["little"]],"h":["little"]},{"i":"p1-16","s":"p1","t":"gap","x":"Give me ___ time, and I will fix it. Ten minutes should do.","f":"\"Time\" is uncountable, and you mean some: a little.","g":"FL","a":[["a little"]],"h":["a little"]},{"i":"p1-17","s":"p1","t":"fix","x":"I need *a few* help with my bike. Do you have a minute?","f":"\"Help\" is uncountable, so it takes \"a little\", not \"a few\".","g":"FL","a":[["a little","some"]],"h":["a little"]},{"i":"p1-18","s":"p1","t":"fix","x":"Sadly, *few* people know how good this band is.","f":"\"Few\" means \"almost none\", and \"sadly\" shows that this is what the speaker means.","g":"FL","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"p2-01","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"My sister goes to work ___, and she sings the whole way.","f":"For transport you say \"by bike\", without an article.","g":"FP","c":"by bike","w":["with the bike","by the bike"]},{"i":"p2-02","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"Somebody asks about your Sunday. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Meals take no article: have breakfast.","g":"FP","c":"We had breakfast at eleven.","w":["We had the breakfast at eleven.","We had a breakfast at eleven."]},{"i":"p2-03","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"My brother plays ___ in a band and ___ in a team. He is never at home.","f":"Instruments take \"the\": play the drums. Sports take no article: play football.","g":"FP","c":"the drums … football","w":["drums … the football","the drums … the football"]},{"i":"p2-04","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"I was so tired that I went to ___ at eight.","f":"\"Go to bed\" is a fixed phrase without an article.","g":"FP","c":"bed","w":["the bed","a bed"]},{"i":"p2-05","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"See you ___! Don't forget the tickets.","f":"\"Next week\" takes no article.","g":"FP","c":"next week","w":["the next week","at next week"]},{"i":"p2-06","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"They are flying to ___ in the summer to visit their aunt in Chicago.","f":"Country names with \"States\" take \"the\": the USA.","g":"GN","c":"the USA","w":["USA","an USA"]},{"i":"p2-07","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"You are doing a geography quiz. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Rivers take \"the\", but cities take no article.","g":"GN","c":"The Rhine flows through Cologne.","w":["Rhine flows through Cologne.","The Rhine flows through the Cologne."]},{"i":"p2-08","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"We spent a week at ___, and it rained every single day.","f":"Lakes take no article: Lake Garda.","g":"GN","c":"Lake Garda","w":["the Lake Garda","a Lake Garda"]},{"i":"p2-09","s":"p2","t":"mc","x":"It is nearly midnight. I think I should go ___.","f":"\"Go home\" is a fixed phrase without \"to\" and without an article.","g":"FP","c":"home","w":["to home","to the home"]},{"i":"p2-10","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"What time do you usually have ___ (dinner)? We eat at six, like pensioners.","f":"Meals take no article: have dinner.","g":"FP","a":[["dinner"]],"h":["dinner"]},{"i":"p2-11","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"My cousin plays ___ (piano) really well, but only one song.","f":"Instruments take \"the\": play the piano.","g":"FP","a":[["the piano"]],"h":["the piano"]},{"i":"p2-12","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"I stayed at ___ (home) all weekend and talked to nobody. It was perfect.","f":"\"At home\" is a fixed phrase without an article.","g":"FP","a":[["home"]],"h":["home"]},{"i":"p2-13","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"She moved to ___ (UK) ___ (last year), and now she says \"lovely\" all the time.","f":"Country names with \"Kingdom\" take \"the\": the UK. \"Last year\" takes no article.","g":"GN","a":[["the UK"],["last year"]],"h":["the UK","last year"]},{"i":"p2-14","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"Have you ever swum in ___ (Atlantic)? It is colder than it looks.","f":"Seas and oceans take \"the\": the Atlantic.","g":"GN","a":[["the Atlantic"]],"h":["the Atlantic"]},{"i":"p2-15","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"My dad goes to ___ (work) by ___ (train), so he reads a lot.","f":"\"Go to work\" and \"by train\" are fixed phrases without an article.","g":"FP","a":[["work"],["train"]],"h":["work","train"]},{"i":"p2-16","s":"p2","t":"gap","x":"We went skiing in ___ (Alps) in February.","f":"Mountain ranges take \"the\": the Alps.","g":"GN","a":[["the Alps"]],"h":["the Alps"]},{"i":"p2-17","s":"p2","t":"fix","x":"We went there *with the car*, and it took four hours.","f":"For transport you say \"by car\", without an article.","g":"FP","a":[["by car","in the car"]],"h":["by car"]},{"i":"p2-18","s":"p2","t":"fix","x":"We spent the summer in *Italy*, and I ate pizza on fourteen days in a row.","f":"Most country names take no article: Italy.","g":"GN","a":[["OK"]],"h":["OK"]},{"i":"pc-01","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"I have ___ good friends, and that is all I need.","f":"\"Friends\" is a plural noun, and the speaker has some: a few.","g":"FL","c":"a few","w":["few","a little"]},{"i":"pc-02","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"There was ___ food at the party, so we ordered pizza on the way home.","f":"\"Food\" is uncountable, and there was almost none: little.","g":"FL","c":"little","w":["a little","few"]},{"i":"pc-03","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"Which sentence means that the speaker is not happy with the number?","f":"\"Few\" means \"almost none\". \"A few\" means \"some\".","g":"FL","c":"Few people liked my post.","w":["A few people liked my post."]},{"i":"pc-04","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"After school I go ___ and play ___ for an hour.","f":"\"Go home\" has no \"to\" and no article. Instruments take \"the\": play the guitar.","g":"FP","c":"home … the guitar","w":["to home … guitar","home … guitar"]},{"i":"pc-05","s":"pc","t":"mc","x":"You are looking at a map of Europe. Which sentence is correct?","f":"Plural country names take \"the\": the Netherlands. Most countries take no article: Germany.","g":"GN","c":"The Netherlands is next to Germany.","w":["Netherlands is next to the Germany.","The Netherlands is next to the Germany."]},{"i":"pc-06","s":"pc","t":"fix","x":"We drove through *the Austria* and arrived in Italy at midnight.","f":"Most country names take no article: Austria.","g":"GN","a":[["Austria"]],"h":["Austria"]},{"i":"pc-07","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"We always have ___ (lunch) at ___ (school). The pasta is a crime.","f":"Meals take no article, and \"at school\" is a fixed phrase without an article.","g":"FP","a":[["lunch"],["school"]],"h":["lunch","school"]},{"i":"pc-08","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"I can't sleep at ___ (night) when there is a full moon.","f":"\"At night\" is a fixed phrase without an article.","g":"FP","a":[["night"]],"h":["night"]},{"i":"pc-09","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"We took a boat down ___ (Thames) and saw nothing because of the fog.","f":"Rivers take \"the\": the Thames.","g":"GN","a":[["the Thames"]],"h":["the Thames"]},{"i":"pc-10","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"My sister plays ___ (basketball) three times a week and ___ (violin) once a year, at Christmas.","f":"Sports take no article: play basketball. Instruments take \"the\": play the violin.","g":"FP","a":[["basketball"],["the violin"]],"h":["basketball","the violin"]},{"i":"pc-11","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"My grandparents live in a small town near ___ (Lake Constance).","f":"Lakes take no article: Lake Constance.","g":"GN","a":[["Lake Constance"]],"h":["Lake Constance"]},{"i":"pc-12","s":"pc","t":"gap","x":"Are you coming to training ___ (next week), or are you still \"ill\"?","f":"\"Next week\" takes no article.","g":"FP","a":[["next week"]],"h":["next week"]}]});
